    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d329">

                <pb facs="0463" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg383"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr.
                            Buck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 358.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At the instance of the Secretary of the
                    Navy, as expressed in his letter of the 20th instant, I have now to instruct you
                    to express to the Government of Japan the cordial appreciation and thanks of
                    this Government for the unusual courtesy shown by Japanese officials and
                    subjects to the squadron of United States ships which was present during the
                    unveiling of the Perry monument on the 14th instant.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
